{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"8d799ae11ae3a41f1eb8cb3e3340db191b16588547bd5f7ac3e9b22863b9821c","digest":{"component_or_area":"repo-isolation session hooks (tests/_isolation.py)","key_entities":["tests/_isolation.py","tests/conftest.py","pytest_sessionfinish","_no_repo_commits","porcelain()","head()","git rev-parse HEAD","git status --porcelain","GIT_PROBE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS","subprocess.TimeoutExpired","tests/unit/test_repo_isolation_guard.py"],"problem_keywords":["subprocess timeout","git probe","repo isolation","session hook","unbounded blocking","pytest teardown"],"propositions":["Read-only Git probes (head and porcelain) in repo-isolation hooks lack subprocess timeout and can block indefinitely, keeping pytest alive after test completion.","When a Git subprocess blocks, the current error-handling code returns None instead of surfacing an explicit failure, masking the timeout condition.","The measured normal repo probe latency (p95 0.0164s, max 0.0610s) permits a fixed 5-second watchdog with >80x safety margin.","The pytest_sessionfinish hook and autouse _no_repo_commits fixture both invoke unguarded Git probes synchronously without timeout.","Timeout failures must be separated from ordinary probe failures (OSError, SubprocessError, non-repository) to explicitly raise subprocess.TimeoutExpired rather than silently returning None."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787073267559328001,"uuid":"4bb3c9d7-fd39-4072-b42d-cab3d28efe7d"}